            "title": "The Restricted Zone (Principal Value Branches)",
            "icon": "✂️",
            "precheck": {
                "question": "If \\( \\sin(\\theta) = 1/2 \\), which of these angles is correct for \\( \\theta \\)?",
                "options": [
                    "30 degrees (\\( \\pi/6 \\))",
                    "150 degrees (\\( 5\\pi/6 \\))",
                    "Actually, both are mathematically correct."
                ],
                "correctIndex": 2,
                "passMessage": "Exactly! That's the problem. An inverse function can only have ONE specific output. If we ask 'What angle gives sine 1/2?', getting two answers breaks the rules of functions!",
                "failMessage": "Both are correct! \\( \\sin(30^\\circ) \\) is 1/2, and \\( \\sin(150^\\circ) \\) is also 1/2. Because multiple angles give the same answer, the backward (inverse) mapping is broken. We have to FIX it by restricting the zone."
            },
            "learn": {
                "paragraphs": [
                    "In Chapter 1, we learned that a function ONLY has an inverse if it is **Bijective (One-One and Onto)**.",
                    "But Trigonometric functions are PERIODIC (They repeat themselves endlessly like a rollercoaster). Because multiple inputs give the same output (Many-One), an 'Inverse' mathematically cannot exist!",
                    "**The Solution:** We must take the endless rollercoaster and *cut out a specific, restricted piece* of the track where it behaves perfectly (One-One). We call this restricted piece the **Principal Value Branch**.",
                    "**The Snipe Scopes (Principal Ranges):**",
                    "1. **The \\( [-\\pi/2, \\pi/2] \\) Family:** \\( \\sin^{-1} x \\), \\( \\csc^{-1} x \\), \\( \\tan^{-1} x \\). The answers for these will ALWAYS fall between -90 and 90 degrees.",
                    "2. **The \\( [0, \\pi] \\) Family:** \\( \\cos^{-1} x \\), \\( \\sec^{-1} x \\), \\( \\cot^{-1} x \\). The answers for these will ALWAYS fall between 0 and 180 degrees (never negative!)."
                ],
                "formulas": [
                    {
                        "rule": "\\( y = \\sin^{-1}(x) \\)",
                        "formula": "Domain: \\( [-1, 1] \\) | Range: \\( [-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}] \\)",
                        "example": "If asked for an angle, it must be between Quadrant IV (negative) and Quadrant I."
                    },
                    {
                        "rule": "\\( y = \\cos^{-1}(x) \\)",
                        "formula": "Domain: \\( [-1, 1] \\) | Range: \\( [0, \\pi] \\)",
                        "example": "If asked for an angle, it must be between Quadrant I and Quadrant II (never negative)."
                    }
                ],
                "boxes": [
