                "paragraphs": [
                    "**1. The Self-Cancelling Rule**",
                    "A function and its inverse neutralize each other. \\( \\sin(\\sin^{-1}(x)) = x \\) AND \\( \\sin^{-1}(\\sin(x)) = x \\).",
                    "**BUT BEWARE!** This ONLY works if the value is inside the Principal Value Branch! If it's outside the restricted zone, you MUST break the angle down using ASTC rules until it fits inside the required branch.",
                    "**2. The Negative Arguments (-x)**",
                    "What happens when you plug a negative number into the inverse functions?",
                    "• **The Direct Negatives (The Odd gang):** \\( \\sin^{-1}(-x) = -\\sin^{-1}(x) \\), \\( \\csc^{-1}(-x) \\), \\( \\tan^{-1}(-x) \\). They just spit the negative straight out to the front.",
