                    "3. \\( \\sec^{-1}(x) + \\csc^{-1}(x) = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\) (For \\( |x| \\ge 1 \\))",
                    "These identities are incredibly powerful shortcuts in calculus and algebra. If a complicated equation asks you to add an arcsin and an arccos of the same messy term, the answer instantly simplifies to just \\( \\pi/2 \\)!"
